00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:18.070
Other to say, other than to say it will be
a tough one.

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:19.670
It's fun to dream.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:25.870
But imagine if both Lindsey Graham and Mitch
McConnell were to lose their seats in the

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:27.450
same election cycle.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:28.450
Unlikely.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.850
But let's work every race like it's potentially
winnable.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:35.680
The fact alone that candidates for historically
noncompetitive Senate seats like South Carolina

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:40.590
and Kentucky are even able to raise this much
money, tells us a lot.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:46.580
It's also sort of frustrating that some candidates
in more competitive States like North Carolina

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:49.500
and Georgia are having trouble raising money.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:51.730
That actually is, is not good.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:54.520
But let's remember the lessons from the midterms
of 2018.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:04:01.380
You know, when, when Democrats took over the
house in 2018, I remember that there was satisfaction

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:05.100
to some degree, but also kind of a feeling
of helplessness.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:08.320
Like what can, what can we really do with
taking over the house?

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:11.970
Trump has executive orders, his cabinet, the
Senate.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:16.180
Well, because Democrats took over the house
in 2018, Donald Trump has been impeached,

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:18.870
becoming only the third president in history
to be impeached.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:20.480
Now that may go nowhere.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:25.289
It may, uh, it certainly is not likely to
lead to Donald Trump's conviction in the Senate.

00:04:25.289 --> 00:04:30.319
It may help to remove Donald Trump by voting
him out in November of 2020.

00:04:30.319 --> 00:04:34.270
But this is why every single one of these
races has to be fought.

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:38.669
Every single one of these Senate races that
could be taken from a Republican has to be

00:04:38.669 --> 00:04:39.669
fought.

00:04:39.669 --> 00:04:43.139
We're only a few seats from a majority in
the Senate.

00:04:43.139 --> 00:04:44.320
I've looked at the numbers.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:46.650
I've told you it's tough.

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:50.199
2022 is more likely, but we won't.

00:04:50.199 --> 00:04:55.260
Given that we're likely to lose one seat in
the Senate, we only need to pick up five in

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:57.169
order to take over control.

00:04:57.169 --> 00:04:59.800
It is not impossible and we should be fighting
for it.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:04.649
The 2018 midterms and Trump now being impeached
are exhibit a as to why this matters.

